nd neighbor signals into the output logits. 2) WHY: Forcing all 355-dimensional tracker signals through a 256-dimensional tabular hidden bottleneck causes lossy compression of tracker identities, whereas direct residual routing allows empirical priors to anchor predictions while domain representations learn fine adjustments. 3) HOW: Extend TrackerRankNet to accept the expanded input dimension, extract or project the tracker-specific prior features through a dedicated residual branch with learnable gating weights, and combine them with direct_logits and prototype similarity logits before returning the final predictions. 4) Interface constraints: Maintain the exact TrackerRankNet constructor signature, initial_bias support, and forward method returning (batch_size, num_classes) logits compatible with AsymmetricFocalRecallLoss."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "Validation Recall@10 plateaued at 0.83246 primarily because feature engineering arbitrarily truncated direct links, neighbor collaborative signals, and Bayesian TLD priors to only top 10-20 trackers, depriving 335 out of 355 trackers of any specific topological or prior signal. Expanding these features to the full 355-dimensional tracker space in data_processing_and_feature_engineering directly provides the missing evidence needed for mid-frequency and regional trackers. Concurrently, updating model_design with a tracker-prior residual connection allows these aligned signals to directly modulate output logits without bottleneck compression, maximizing ranking performance.",
