{"reason": "Validation Recall@10 plateaued early at 0.8354 despite training loss dropping, caused by the severe information bottleneck of compressing all features into a 256-dimensional hidden layer while discarding 97% of direct tracker links and ignoring 1-hop link graph neighbor consensus. Data processing and feature engineering is the exact place to construct the missing 355-dimensional structural signals from the link graph and full TLD base rates. Model design is the essential component to replace the single-stream bottleneck with a dual-stream architecture featuring structural feature dropout and a context-gated bypass directly aligned with the 355 tracker targets. These two modifications directly unblock the model's ability to rank regional and community-specific trackers without losing contextual generalization on low-degree domains.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "1) WHAT: Engineer four 355-dimensional tracker-aligned structural feature blocks: full 355-tracker direct link presence indicators, 1-hop out-neighbor training tracker consensus distributions, 1-hop in-neighbor training tracker consensus distributions, and full 355-tracker TLD-conditional empirical base rates. 2) WHY: The current pipeline only evaluates links to 10 trackers and 5 TLD priors, completely discarding topological community membership and web tracker adoption patterns across the 3.0 GB link graph. 3) HOW: Build sparse adjacency operators between domains and training labels using SciPy CSR matrices to compute normalized neighbor tracker distributions (A_out * Y_train and A_in * Y_train), map destination domain IDs to all 355 tracker IDs for direct link detection, and compute smoothed 355-dim TLD-conditional tracker likelihood vectors, concatenating these 1420 structural features onto the tabular contextual feature matrix. 4) Interface constraints: Preserve extract_feature_matrix output schema, maintaining train_features_df, val_features_df, test_features_df, num_features, and prior_log_odds for seamless downstream consumption.", "model_design": "1) WHAT: Upgrade TrackerGatedRankNet into a Graph-Augmented Dual-Stream Network with a Tracker-Aligned Gated Bypass and structural feature dropout (p = 0.25). 2) WHY: Passing high-dimensional label-aligned graph consensus through a single 256-dim bottleneck causes severe information loss, while high-degree hub dominance risks causing the network to ignore contextual signals on isolated test domains. 3) HOW: In TrackerGatedRankNet, split input features into contextual and structural streams; route contextual features through BatchNorm, linear projection, and SwishGLU residual blocks to generate domain embeddings h and logits logit_ctx, apply structural dropout to the 1420 structural features before projecting via a linear layer directly to logit_struct, and dynamically fuse via a context-conditioned sigmoid gate logits = logit_ctx + sigmoid(W_g * h + b_g) * logit_struct before the LabelInteractionModule. 4) Interface constraints: Retain TrackerGatedRankNet class name, forward(x) signature, prior_bias output initialization, and TopKAsymmetricRecallLoss loss interface."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
