    "model_design": "1) WHAT: Upgrade TrackerGatedRankNet into a Graph-Augmented Dual-Stream Network with a Tracker-Aligned Gated Bypass and structural feature dropout (p = 0.25). 2) WHY: Passing high-dimensional label-aligned graph consensus through a single 256-dim bottleneck causes severe information loss, while high-degree hub dominance risks causing the network to ignore contextual signals on isolated test domains. 3) HOW: In TrackerGatedRankNet, split input features into contextual and structural streams; route contextual features through BatchNorm, linear projection, and SwishGLU residual blocks to generate domain embeddings h and logits logit_ctx, apply structural dropout to the 1420 structural features before projecting via a linear layer directly to logit_struct, and dynamically fuse via a context-conditioned sigmoid gate logits = logit_ctx + sigmoid(W_g * h + b_g) * logit_struct before the LabelInteractionModule. 4) Interface constraints: Retain TrackerGatedRankNet class name, forward(x) signature, prior_bias output initialization, and TopKAsymmetricRecallLoss loss interface."
