{"reason": "Validation Recall@10 peaked early at 0.8431 at epoch 6 before regressing to 0.8420, caused by severe over-parameterization in the dense 1420-to-355 structural projection (504k weights) and loss misalignment from penalizing top-15 negatives equally regardless of rank. Data processing and feature engineering is the right place to extract tracker-level metadata attributes from trackers.tsv and compute the symmetric normalized tracker co-occurrence adjacency matrix strictly from training labels. Model design is the critical component to introduce tracker-aligned grouped channel projections, embed tracker metadata, diffuse predictions over the empirical co-occurrence graph, and focus negative ranking margins strictly on the top-10 competition threshold. Training evaluation provides the required optimization stabilization by introducing a 1-epoch linear learning rate warmup to protect calibrated priors from early gradient shock.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "1) WHAT: Extract categorical metadata indices (category, country, and parent brand) for all 355 trackers from trackers.tsv, and compute the symmetric normalized tracker co-occurrence adjacency matrix strictly from train_labels_csr. 2) WHY: The current pipeline only extracts tracker IDs while discarding rich tracker attributes and co-occurrence graphs, depriving the model of structural ecosystem relationships that group regional and functional trackers together. 3) HOW: Encode tracker category, country, and brand into integer index tensors of length 355 (mapping unknown/missing values to dedicated index 0) and construct the symmetric normalized co-occurrence matrix A_norm = D^{-1/2} (Y_train^T Y_train) D^{-1/2} with self-loops on the training split. 4) Interface constraints: Preserve existing dataset variables (train_features_df, val_features_df, test_features_df, num_features, and prior_log_odds) while outputting tracker_meta_indices and norm_co_occurrence for downstream model consumption.", "model_design": "1) WHAT: Upgrade TrackerGatedRankNet with a tracker-aligned grouped structural projection, tracker metadata embeddings, and empirical co-occurrence graph diffusion, while focusing TopKAsymmetricRecallLoss on rank-discounted top-10 hard negatives. 2) WHY: The 1420-to-355 dense structural projection contains 504k weights that learn spurious cross-tracker noise, while the unconstrained classifier ignores tracker semantics and top-15 unweighted negative ranking distorts the crucial top-10 evaluation boundary. 3) HOW: Reshape the 1420 structural features to (batch, 355, 4) and project each tracker's 4 dedicated channels to a single structural logit using per-tracker parameters (reducing structural weights by 99.7%), replace the unconstrained classifier with domain-tracker dot-product affinity using category/country/brand embeddings, replace the random low-rank module with empirical graph diffusion (logits + alpha * (logits @ A_norm)), and update the ranking loss to penalize top-10 negatives weighted by 1 / log2(rank + 2). 4) Interface constraints: Retain TrackerGatedRankNet class name, constructor compatibility with in_features and prior_bias, and TopKAsymmetricRecallLoss forward signature returning a scalar loss.", "training_evaluation": "1) WHAT: Add a 1-epoch linear learning rate warmup before the cosine annealing scheduler and preserve best-epoch validation checkpointing based on Recall@10. 2) WHY: Randomly initialized tracker metadata embeddings and grouped projections cause high initial gradient volatility that disrupts pre-calibrated prior log-odds and causes early metric degradation. 3) HOW: Wrap the optimizer with a linear warmup scheduler scaling learning rate from 1e-4 to 1e-3 over epoch 1 before transitioning to CosineAnnealingLR for epochs 2 through 12, tracking validation Recall@10 every epoch and restoring best weights for inference. 4) Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10 function signature, evaluation batch size (1024), patience logic, and final submission file formatting writing domain_id and tracking_domain_id to submission.csv and submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
