{"reason": "Validation Recall@10 reached 0.8419 in just 4 minutes with loss steadily decreasing through epoch 12, demonstrating that the model was prematurely halted while still learning. Furthermore, peripheral evaluation domains suffer from zero-coverage 1-hop consensus, the structural linear combination lacks non-linear capacity, and the single-scalar co-occurrence diffusion cannot differentiate tracker-specific diffusion intensities. Informed by historical experiments that succeeded by maintaining parameter efficiency while avoiding dense over-parameterization, modifying data processing, model design, and training evaluation jointly resolves coverage gaps, introduces tracker-calibrated non-linear interactions, and allows full parameter convergence.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "1) WHAT: Remove the 200,000 domain cap to utilize all non-test training domains, compute a 2-hop degree-normalized out-neighbor tracker consensus matrix via sparse link-graph multiplication, precompute the 2-hop normalized tracker co-occurrence matrix A_norm_2, and assemble 5 tracker-aligned structural blocks (1,775 dimensions total). 2) WHY: Peripheral web domains frequently lack direct 1-hop edges to labeled training domains, resulting in empty consensus vectors that starve the structural stream of evidence. 3) HOW: Build the inter-domain evaluation link adjacency matrix to propagate 1-hop out-neighbor consensus to 2-hop neighbors with row degree normalization, compute A_norm_2 = A_norm @ A_norm from training co-occurrences, and concatenate direct links, 1-hop out/in consensus, 2-hop out consensus, and TLD priors. 4) Interface constraints: Retain existing feature pipeline outputs including train_features_df, val_features_df, test_features_df, num_features, prior_log_odds, tracker_meta_indices, and pass norm_co_occurrence and norm_co_occurrence_2 to the model.", "model_design": "1) WHAT: Replace the rigid per-tracker linear combination with a shared Non-Linear Structural Channel Interaction MLP (5 channels projected to 32 dimensions with SiLU, LayerNorm, and tracker embedding modulation before scalar projection) and upgrade empirical diffusion into a Parametric Multi-Hop Co-occurrence Graph Filter with per-tracker learnable vectors alpha_1 and alpha_2 for 1-hop and 2-hop diffusion. 2) WHY: Linear projection cannot capture non-linear structural rules (such as high-confidence direct link overrides versus synergistic consensus support), while a single global diffusion scalar over-diffuses ubiquitous trackers across unrelated domains; sharing the channel MLP avoids the catastrophic over-parameterization observed in prior failed experiments. 3) HOW: In TrackerGatedRankNet, reshape structural inputs to (batch, 355, 5), apply structural dropout (p=0.25), pass through a shared 2-layer MLP conditioned on tracker metadata embeddings to obtain logit_struct, and compute final logits as fused_logits + alpha_1 * (fused_logits @ A_norm) + alpha_2 * (fused_logits @ A_norm_2) with alpha parameters initialized at 0.05. 4) Interface constraints: Maintain TrackerGatedRankNet class name, constructor compatibility with in_features, prior_bias, and tracker_meta_indices, and return (batch_size, 355) logits compatible with TopKAsymmetricRecallLoss.", "training_evaluation": "1) WHAT: Increase total training epochs from 12 to 20 with an extended Warmup-CosineAnnealing schedule and increase early stopping patience to 5 epochs. 2) WHY: Execution logs showed validation loss dropping continuously from 3.28 to 3.19 at epoch 12 within only 4 minutes, indicating the network had not reached convergence on the training objective. 3) HOW: Configure SequentialLR with 1 epoch of linear warmup followed by CosineAnnealingLR for epochs 2 through 20 (eta_min=1e-5), track validation Recall@10 at each epoch to checkpoint the best model weights, and generate final test predictions mapped to tracking_domain_id. 4) Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10 function signature, evaluation batch size (1024), and output submission formatting with domain_id and tracking_domain_id saved to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
